How would you make ArrayList thread-safe in production?
▼
Three options, with trade-offs:

Collections.synchronizedList(list) — wraps every method in synchronized. Simple but coarse lock, poor throughput under contention.

CopyOnWriteArrayList — creates a new array on every write. Ideal when reads vastly outnumber writes (e.g., listeners, observer lists). Very expensive writes.

ReadWriteLock + ArrayList — custom wrapper with ReentrantReadWriteLock. Best for mixed read/write if you control the code.

// CopyOnWriteArrayList — best for read-heavy
List<String> safe = new CopyOnWriteArrayList<>();
