What happens to memory when you remove elements?
▼
ArrayList does NOT shrink automatically. After removing elements, the backing array retains its capacity. Removed slots are set to null (to allow GC of the object), but the array slots remain allocated. Call trimToSize() explicitly to reclaim space. This is a common memory leak pattern in long-lived lists.

// After bulk removal, the array stays at old capacity
list.removeIf(e -> e > 1000); // size drops, capacity unchanged
list.trimToSize();             // now capacity == size
