subList() — what's the trap?
▼
list.subList(from, to) returns a view, not a copy. Modifying the subList modifies the original, and modifying the original after taking a subList throws ConcurrentModificationException. To get a safe copy: new ArrayList<>(list.subList(1, 4)).

List<Integer> sub = list.subList(1, 4); // view, not copy
sub.clear();          // modifies original list!
list.add(99);         // now sub.get(0) throws CME
